<%# Workflow — how an order moves through the PMS, read top to bottom. Built
    from the live catalogue rather than written out by hand, so it cannot
    drift from what the engine actually does when somebody edits a step. %>
<div class="container-fluid py-4" id="pfRoot">
  <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start mb-3 flex-wrap gap-2">
    <div>
      <h3 class="mb-0 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fas fa-diagram-project me-2"></i>Workflow — <span id="pf_nsteps">…</span> Steps</h3>
      <div class="text-muted small">How every order moves through the PMS, from the punch to dispatch. Read it top to bottom.</div>
    </div>
    <button class="btn btn-outline-dark smooth-ui text-dark fw-bold" onclick="refreshBoard(this, pf_load, 'pmsFlow')"><i class="fas fa-sync-alt me-1"></i> Refresh</button>
  </div>

  <div class="card shadow smooth-ui mb-3">
    <div class="card-body">
      <h6 class="fw-bold mb-3"><i class="fas fa-circle-info me-2"></i>How it works, in five points</h6>
      <div class="row g-3 row-cols-1 row-cols-md-5">
        <div class="col"><div class="border rounded p-3 h-100">
          <div class="badge bg-dark mb-2">1</div>
          <div class="fw-semibold mb-1">Order comes in</div>
          <div class="small text-muted">Punched on the New Order form. It joins the board only if it was punched on or after the start date in Step Settings.</div>
        </div></div>
        <div class="col"><div class="border rounded p-3 h-100">
          <div class="badge bg-dark mb-2">2</div>
          <div class="fw-semibold mb-1">Step 1 opens</div>
          <div class="small text-muted">Due = order date + TAT, counted from 10:00. With no TAT the step still opens, just without a date.</div>
        </div></div>
        <div class="col"><div class="border rounded p-3 h-100">
          <div class="badge bg-dark mb-2">3</div>
          <div class="fw-semibold mb-1">Steps run in order</div>
          <div class="small text-muted">One after another. A step whose condition says no is skipped and the next opens straight away.</div>
        </div></div>
        <div class="col"><div class="border rounded p-3 h-100">
          <div class="badge bg-dark mb-2">4</div>
          <div class="fw-semibold mb-1">Done &rarr; next step</div>
          <div class="small text-muted">The actual is recorded with who marked it, and the next step opens with Due = that actual + its TAT.</div>
        </div></div>
        <div class="col"><div class="border rounded p-3 h-100">
          <div class="badge bg-dark mb-2">5</div>
          <div class="fw-semibold mb-1">Past the date &rarr; Delayed</div>
          <div class="small text-muted">It turns red on the board and marking it done asks why it was late. A step with no TAT is never called late.</div>
        </div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card shadow smooth-ui mb-3">
    <div class="card-body">
      <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center flex-wrap gap-2 mb-1">
        <h6 class="mb-0 fw-bold"><i class="fas fa-sitemap me-2"></i>Flow chart</h6>
        <div class="small">
          <span class="badge bg-success-subtle text-success-emphasis">Always</span>
          <span class="badge bg-info-subtle text-info-emphasis">Only sometimes</span>
          <span class="badge bg-light text-muted border">Off</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-muted small mb-3">Steps open one after another, top to bottom. A coloured step runs only when its condition is met — otherwise it is skipped and the next one opens.</div>
      <div id="pf_chart"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row g-3 mb-3">
    <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
      <div class="card shadow smooth-ui h-100">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h6 class="fw-bold mb-3"><i class="far fa-calendar me-2"></i>How the due date is worked out</h6>
          <ul class="small mb-3">
            <li><b>Step 1:</b> order date + TAT, counted from 10:00.</li>
            <li><b>Every next step:</b> the previous step's actual + its TAT.</li>
            <li>Done <b>after 18:00</b> &rarr; the TAT counts from 10:00 the next working day.</li>
            <li>Done <b>before 10:00</b> &rarr; it counts from 10:00 the same day.</li>
            <li><b>Sunday is a holiday.</b> A TAT is in working days, so a 3 day step that crosses a Sunday is still 3 days of work.</li>
            <li><b>No TAT set</b> &rarr; no due date, and the step is never late.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm mb-0">
              <thead class="table-dark"><tr><th colspan="2" class="small">EXAMPLE</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody class="small">
                <tr><td>Order punched</td><td class="text-end fw-semibold">Mon 14 Sep, 3:00 pm</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Step 1 due (TAT 1 day)</td><td class="text-end fw-semibold">Tue 15 Sep, 3:00 pm</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Step 1 done</td><td class="text-end fw-semibold">Thu 24 Sep, 2:30 pm</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Step 2 due (TAT 4 days)</td><td class="text-end fw-semibold">Tue 29 Sep, 2:30 pm</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="text-muted" colspan="2">Sun 27 Sep was skipped, so 4 working days lands on the 29th.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
      <div class="card shadow smooth-ui h-100">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h6 class="fw-bold mb-3"><i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation me-2"></i>Rules worth knowing</h6>
          <div class="border-start border-4 border-danger ps-3 mb-3">
            <div class="fw-semibold small">Late needs a reason</div>
            <div class="small text-muted">Marking a step done past its date asks why, and will not save without one. Asked later it would be a guess.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="border-start border-4 border-warning ps-3 mb-3">
            <div class="fw-semibold small">A step with no TAT is not late</div>
            <div class="small text-muted">It is unmeasured. The board counts those separately so nobody is marked down against a number that was never set.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="border-start border-4 border-info ps-3 mb-3">
            <div class="fw-semibold small">Conditions are read when the step is about to open</div>
            <div class="small text-muted">Not at the punch. Nobody yet knows at punch whether the job needs a die, so deciding early would freeze a guess into the order.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="border-start border-4 border-secondary ps-3">
            <div class="fw-semibold small">Older orders are left alone</div>
            <div class="small text-muted">Only orders punched on or after the start date get steps. The thousands already in the system stay as they are.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card shadow smooth-ui">
    <div class="card-body">
      <h6 class="fw-bold mb-1"><i class="fas fa-table-list me-2"></i>All steps at a glance</h6>
      <div class="text-muted small mb-3">A step that does not apply to an order is skipped and the next opens straight away.</div>
      <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table table-sm align-middle mcard mb-0">
          <thead class="table-dark">
            <tr><th>#</th><th>Step</th><th>When it applies</th><th>Who</th><th>TAT</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="pf_table"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
var PF_COND = {
  revision: 'Client asked for changes',
  guest_name: 'Guest list / addressing given',
  die: 'Die needed',
  block: 'Block needed',
  edges: 'Edges needed',
  laser: 'Laser cutting needed',
  output: 'Output needed',
};

function pf_esc(s) {
  return String(s === null || s === undefined ? '' : s)
    .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
    .replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
}

async function pf_load() {
  try {
    var r = await fetch('/api/pms/steps');
    var j = await r.json();
    if (!j.success) throw new Error(j.error || 'Could not load.');
    var steps = j.steps || [];
    document.getElementById('pf_nsteps').textContent = steps.filter(function (s) {
      return s.is_active;
    }).length;
    pf_chart(steps);
    pf_table(steps);
  } catch (e) {
    document.getElementById('pf_chart').innerHTML =
      '<div class="text-danger">' + pf_esc(e.message) + '</div>';
  }
}

function pf_arrow() {
  return '<div class="text-center text-muted" style="line-height:1;">'
    + '<i class="fas fa-arrow-down"></i></div>';
}

function pf_chart(steps) {
  var html = '<div class="text-center mb-2"><span class="badge rounded-pill px-3 py-2" '
    + 'style="background:#4b5320;">Order punched · joins the board</span></div>' + pf_arrow();

  steps.forEach(function (s) {
    var off = !s.is_active;
    var cond = !!s.condition_key;
    var cls = off ? 'bg-light border' : cond
      ? 'bg-info-subtle border border-info-subtle'
      : 'bg-success-subtle border border-success-subtle';

    html += '<div class="rounded p-2 px-3 my-1 ' + cls + (off ? ' opacity-50' : '') + '">'
      + '<div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start gap-2 flex-wrap">'
      + '<div><span class="badge bg-dark me-2">' + s.step_order + '</span>'
      + '<span class="fw-semibold">' + pf_esc(s.name) + '</span>'
      + (off ? ' <span class="badge bg-secondary ms-1">off</span>' : '')
      + (cond ? '<div class="small text-info-emphasis mt-1"><i class="fas fa-code-branch me-1"></i>'
        + 'Only if: ' + pf_esc(PF_COND[s.condition_key] || s.condition_key)
        + ' — otherwise skipped</div>' : '')
      + (s.note ? '<div class="small text-muted">' + pf_esc(s.note) + '</div>' : '')
      + '</div>'
      + '<div class="text-end small text-muted" style="min-width:9rem;">'
      + '<div><i class="far fa-user me-1"></i>' + pf_esc(s.doer_role || 'nobody set') + '</div>'
      + (s.tat_days === null
        ? '<div class="text-warning-emphasis"><i class="far fa-clock me-1"></i>no TAT</div>'
        : '<div><i class="far fa-clock me-1"></i>TAT ' + s.tat_days + ' day'
          + (s.tat_days === 1 ? '' : 's') + '</div>')
      + '</div></div></div>' + pf_arrow();
  });

  html += '<div class="text-center mt-2"><span class="badge rounded-pill px-3 py-2 bg-success">'
    + 'Order completed</span></div>';
  document.getElementById('pf_chart').innerHTML = html;
}

function pf_table(steps) {
  document.getElementById('pf_table').innerHTML = steps.map(function (s) {
    return '<tr' + (s.is_active ? '' : ' class="opacity-50"') + '>'
      + '<td class="text-muted">' + s.step_order + '</td>'
      + '<td class="fw-semibold">' + pf_esc(s.name) + '</td>'
      + '<td>' + (s.condition_key
        ? '<span class="badge bg-info-subtle text-info-emphasis border border-info-subtle">'
          + pf_esc(PF_COND[s.condition_key] || s.condition_key) + '</span>'
        : '<span class="text-muted small">Always</span>') + '</td>'
      + '<td class="small">' + pf_esc(s.doer_role || '—') + '</td>'
      + '<td class="small">' + (s.tat_days === null
        ? '<span class="text-warning-emphasis">not set</span>'
        : s.tat_days + 'd') + '</td></tr>';
  }).join('');
  if (window.mcardStamp) mcardStamp(document.getElementById('pf_table').closest('table'));
}

pf_load();
</script>
